This agreement covers Dotlink 0.1.0-beta.23 and later: the desktop app for Windows, macOS and
Linux, and the Android app. By installing or using Dotlink you agree to it. Dotlink
0.1.0-beta.22 and earlier were released under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later, and those versions stay under it.

1. Using Dotlink

   You may download, install and use Dotlink on any number of devices, for personal or work
   use, free of charge. Without a license, the desktop app keeps every feature working; after
   a 30-day trial it shows that it is unregistered and, from time to time, a reminder to buy a
   license.

2. Licenses

   A license is bought from the store linked in the app. It is for one person, and covers
   every computer that person uses. A license removes the "Unregistered" label and the
   reminder. It does not expire, and covers later versions of Dotlink for as long as they
   accept license keys of the kind you received. Keep your license key to yourself: sharing
   it, publishing it or selling it is not allowed, and a key that is shared may be revoked in
   a later version.

3. What you may not do

   You may not:
   - sell, rent or redistribute Dotlink, or include it in another product, without written
     permission (linking to the official download page is fine);
   - make, share or use license keys that were not issued for Dotlink's store;
   - modify, decompile or reverse engineer Dotlink to remove or bypass the license check, the
     "Unregistered" label or the reminder, except where the law allows it regardless of this
     agreement.

4. Third-party software

   Dotlink includes or downloads third-party software under its own licenses, for example the
   fonts bundled with the Android app and scrcpy (Apache License 2.0), which Dotlink downloads
   for Cast. Those licenses apply to those parts.

5. Privacy

   Dotlink works on your own network or USB cable. It has no account and sends nothing to its
   maker, except checking GitHub for new releases.

6. No warranty

   Dotlink is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
   fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. Dotlink can control the computer it
   runs on (shell, keyboard and mouse, files) for the devices you pair with it; you are
   responsible for which devices you pair.

7. Limitation of liability

   To the extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any damages arising from the use
   of or inability to use Dotlink, including lost data or profits, even if told they may
   happen. Where liability can't be excluded, it is limited to the amount you paid for your
   license.

8. Ending this agreement

   This agreement ends if you break it; you must then stop using Dotlink. Sections 6 and 7
   stay in force after it ends.

